# Maya's business idea (draft v1)

Problem: Small restaurants in the Bay Area run on thin margins and juggle scheduling, inventory, and POS tools that were built for chains. Owners like my parents spend hours each week on manual ordering and staff schedules.

Idea: A simple, cheap software tool for independent restaurants that handles supplier ordering and prep/inventory forecasting from their own sales data.

Why me: I grew up working in my parents' 40-seat restaurant in San Jose, and I have the CS and web/ML skills to build it.

First step: Interview 10 local owners, build a clickable prototype, then run a pilot with one restaurant (my parents' place is the first test).

